From 4448266f3447a19de3d9b8f70b0ad99a19bd88ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:34:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 69/71] tls: the server's certificate verified as Xray verifies
 it: other names, a pinned CA

certificate_server_name is a list of names: the server's certificate is verified against the
roots (the system's, or those of certificate) for any of them, in place of server_name, which the
handshake still sends; with disable_sni nothing is sent and the names verify. It is Xray's
verifyPeerCertByName ("vcn" of a link): a server reached by one name (a front, an address) with
a certificate for another.

certificate_sha256 (0102) pins a whole certificate: upstream takes the leaf only. Here it also
takes a CA of the chain above the leaf, as Xray takes pinnedPeerCertSha256 (verifyChain,
foundCA): the chain is then verified to that CA alone, by certificate_server_name or the server
name. A pinned leaf is taken by itself, whatever its names and issuer. Both together work as in
Xray.

Feature names: tls.certificate_sha256 (with the pinned CA), tls.certificate_server_name.

- The std and uTLS clients verify in VerifyPeerCertificate (InsecureSkipVerify, as upstream's
  pins do), set per server name in SetServerName and kept by Clone; ECH, kTLS, shadowtls and the
  QUIC clients that take the std configuration go through it. With a pin or names, disable_sni no
  longer verifies the server name against the roots as well (upstream refused a pinned
  self-signed server without SNI on the std client).
- certificate_server_name is refused with insecure and with an empty name; unavailable with
  REALITY, which checks its own key (the REALITY client installs its own verification per
  connection), and in the apple and windows engines. naive refuses it and both pins: Cronet
  verifies by the server name only.
- The link decoder: pcs and pinSHA256 are kept with insecure (Hysteria checks its pin then, and
  Xray has no insecure any more), which is dropped; dashes are taken out of a hash too; vcn becomes
  certificate_server_name unless every name is the server name; the XHTTP download reads its own
  pinnedPeerCertSha256 and verifyPeerCertByName; naive gets neither, with a warning.

Pdk-Feature: certificate-server-name
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 07
